  "id": "spine-extension",
  "name": "Spine Extension",
  "definition": "A strict bilateral fixed-path lumbar isolation performed on the MedX lumbar-extension machine while the thighs, distal femurs, feet, and posterior pelvis are restrained so the pelvis cannot lift or rotate. The lumbar spine extends from the machine's 72-degree full-flexion reference to its 0-degree full-extension reference, holds for one second, and returns under control. Fisher directly anchors the restraint system, range, cadence, and lumbar-extensor training outcome. The sole primary is the newly truthful lumbarExtensors region representing erector spinae and multifidus. BodyModel.scn has no matching surface, so the exercise earns exact-region volume and development credit without painting quadratus lumborum or posterior serratus as substitutes. Other machines, unsupported back extensions, Roman-chair and 45-degree variants, hip-driven repetitions, reverse hypers, floor supermans, isometrics, limited ranges, and pain-treatment prescriptions remain outside this contract.",
  "evidenceRefs": [
    "christophy-2012-lumbar-spine",
    "fisher-2018-isolated-lumbar-extension"
  ],
